/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  batch13_breakthrough_co2  --  CO2/He breakthrough on a zeolite-13X bed.

  THE A3 anchor case (spec 2026-07-12): a 0.5 m isothermal fixed bed of
  zeolite 13X, fed 15% CO2 in helium at u = 0.05 m/s superficial, 1 bar,
  298 K.  Helium carries NO isotherm record on 13X -> announced inert
  CARRIER, transported but never adsorbed, closed by difference from the
  constant c_tot = P/(RT).  At 15% CO2 this is NOT a dilute approximation:
  the constant-(u, P, T) closure implies He at the net uptake rate, and
  the campaign books it as a NAMED INLET STREAM of the bed, `carrierMakeUp`
  ("carrier implied by the constant-(u, P, T) assumption"), so mass and
  element balances close and the stream is the explanation; its size is
  the assumption's size (KPIs carrier_fabricated_mol, carrier_makeup_rel);
  the genuinely clean transport anchor is batch14.  The engine announces, BEFORE integrating, where the front must
  arrive:

      q*(c_in) = 5*9*0.15/(1 + 9*0.15) = 2.872340426 mol/kg
      R_f  = eps + rho_b q* / c_in     = 304.0512509
      t_st = (L/u) R_f                 = 3040.512509 s
      u_sh = u/R_f                     = 1.644459605e-4 m/s

  The front this run computes (convectionScheme vanLeer, the stated
  default since C375; nCells = 100):

      t_b(5%) = 2934.069 s    t_50 = 3035.101 s    t_b(95%) = 3165.565 s
      5-95 % width 231.5 s; unused bed length L(1 - t_b/t_st) = 0.0175 m
      INT(1 - c_out/c_in)dt = t_st to 3e-8  (telescopic FV conservation)
      ledger mass closure at round-off (IN/OUT rows of the SAME ODE)

  That is the PHYSICAL front within the stated tolerance: the mesh-
  converged front (Richardson, 800/1600 cells) has t_b(5%) = 2939.26 s,
  width 219.6 s, unused length 0.0167 m, so at 100 cells van Leer is
  0.18 % early on t_b and 5.4 % wide (gate check_fixed_bed_scheme; the
  width converges at order ~2).  THE COMPARISON A STUDENT CAN REPRODUCE:
  declare `convectionScheme upwind;` and the first-order scheme adds its
  numerical dispersion v dz/2 = 3.1e-4 m2/s, 1.25 times the physical
  Dax/eps = 2.5e-4 (the run announces it), and the front becomes the
  grid's: t_b(5%) = 2890.669 s, t_50 = 3036.448 s, t_b(95%) = 3204.166 s,
  width 313.5 s, unused length 0.0246 m (the A3 anchors of anchors_a3.py,
  FV N = 100, observed order ~1.03-1.05 -- batch15 is that mesh study).
  The stoichiometric time does not move with either scheme or mesh.

  Numerics: conservative FV, nCells = 100 DECLARED, Danckwerts inlet as the
  imposed face flux u*c_in, outlet
  dc/dz = 0.  u, P, T are DECLARED constants of this phase, and the price
  is said OUT LOUD: the real velocity drops ~15% across the uptake zone,
  so the constant-u closure FABRICATES carrier (He) at exactly the net
  uptake rate (9.19 mol here) -- announced in the run header, pinned as
  the KPI carrier_fabricated_mol and booked as the `carrierMakeUp` inlet
  stream of the campaign ledger; Ergun (`flowModel ergun`) needs no such
  stream, and the energy balance of this closure stays UNAVAILABLE (named).

  Log: run header prints the hypotheses, the derived rho_p, Pe = 250, the
  Gershgorin step bound term by term, the scheme's numerical dispersion
  and the stiffness verdict; the initial profile lands in 0/bed.profile
  (the later <t>/bed.profile files are erased by the instant writer -- a
  defect recorded in docs/design/fixed-bed-numerics-c375.md); trajectory.csv carries c_out, y_out,
  qbar and the per-species ledger closure.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        bed;
        type        fixedBedAdsorber;

        operation
        {
            adsorbent   zeolite13X;    // by NAME -- vendored under constant/
                                       // (case-local copy; tRef = 298 K
                                       // anchor, see the record header)
            L           0.5   m;       // bed length
            area        0.01  m2;      // cross-section
            eps         0.4;           // interparticle void fraction
            u           0.05  m/s;     // superficial, CONSTANT DECLARED (A4: Ergun)
            T           298   K;       // isothermal DECLARED (A4: energy)
            P           1     bar;     // CONSTANT DECLARED
            Dax  [0 2 -1 0 0]  1e-4;   // m2/s -- axial dispersion DECLARED
                                       // (Pe = 250; correlation = A4)
            nCells      100;           // axial mesh DECLARED -- absent = FATAL

            feed    { molarComposition { CO2 0.15; He 0.85; } }
            initial { molarComposition { He  1.0; } }   // clean bed: q = 0

            kLDF                       // EQUIPMENT/SAMPLE data: lives in the
            {                          // case, never in a standards .dat
                basis    solidFilm;    // dq/dt = k*(q* - q)
                scope    "2 mm 13X beads, teaching bed RUN-A3-ANCHOR";
                source   "declared spec value (A3 anchor); Glueckauf k = 15 De/rp^2 gives the order";
                k
                {
                    CO2  [0 0 -1 0 0]  0.05;   // 1/s
                }
            }
        }
    }
);
